  "body": "Right now there is no way to call `Body#formData` on arbitrary user input without potentially causing an OOM. It would be great if we could constrain the `formData` parser so it stops parsing if a body exceeds a certain size.\r\n\r\nExample API:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst form = req.formData({ maxSize: 10_000_000 /* 10MB */ })\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf the body size exceeds the max size, a `QuotaExceededError` `DOMException` should be thrown.\r\n\r\nThis might make sense for `.text()`, `.blob()`, `.arrayBuffer()`, and `.json()` also.",
